  "worked_solution": "Let's try and solve using the square root method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-5)^{2}-8 & =2n \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =2n+8 \\\\ \\sqrt{(x-5)^{2}} & =\\sqrt{2n+8} \\\\ |x-5| & =\\sqrt{2n+8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation will have no real solutions if the expression under the square root is negative, which gives the following condition:\n\n$$\n2n+8<0\n$$\n\nWe solve this inequality for $n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n+8 & <0 \\\\ 2n & <-8 \\\\ n & <\\frac{-8}{2} \\\\ n & <-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, any value of $n$ that is less than $-4$ will give an equation with no real solutions.",
